   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;text-align:left;">The aggregate amount of time deposits issued in excess of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation ("FDIC") insured limit, currently <em style="font: inherit;">$250,000,</em> at&#160;<em style="font: inherit;"> June 30, 2026</em> and <em style="font: inherit;"> December 31, 2025</em>, was&#160;$<ix:nonFraction id="c148825176" contextRef="i_2026-06-30" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:TimeDepositsAtOrAboveFDICInsuranceLimit" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">175.5</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction id="c148825177" contextRef="i_2025-12-31" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:TimeDepositsAtOrAboveFDICInsuranceLimit" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">164.2</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively.</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;text-align:left;">&#160;</p>
